## 3. Test Plan

Execution environment L: current local darwin-x64, Node 22.22.3 at /usr/local/Cellar/node@22/22.22.3/bin/node, SDK server/client 2.0.0 with lock integrity. Check versions again when running. The final candidate is the retained implementation plus the narrowly authorized baseline change and regenerated/package payloads, bound by new manifest digests and retained diff. The existing disposable candidate /private/tmp/agdf-contract-candidate-3ahp_a7h and evidence/implementation-01/ remain historical inputs; capture the final snapshot after all required generation succeeds. The final digest is not yet available. Record it before any native session, then keep it constant through that evaluation. Never test against the old installed serving plugin and call it the candidate.

Use disposable fixture targets and an isolated candidate assembly. Preserve foreign working files and source/control data. Build with current scripts, in their documented order. The canonical build may stop on stale host evidence: inspect the diagnostic and use its existing owner; never rewrite completed observations or silently requalify hosts. No lockfile, dependency, SDK, version or MCP threshold change is authorized. The sole packaging-baseline exception is plugins/agdf/meta/copilot-payload-baseline.json max_bytes 3495133 -> 3509461, retaining max_files 397, zero headroom, mapping/digest checks and existing profile exclusions. The measured increase is exactly 14328 bytes (about 0.41%); TP_BASELINE_DECISION-01.md records the owner decision. After applying this exact baseline, all required profile generation and package checks must pass on the final candidate; any larger payload returns to TP clarification, with no further increase inferred. Historical native/performance baselines remain unchanged. Installed dependencies may be reused only when locked versions/integrity match. Missing dependencies/network permission is reported and resolved through the existing environment owner.

### Routes and exact owners

- R1: node packages/mcp-server/test/protocol.test.js and node packages/mcp-server/test/contract.test.js, extending these existing owners for modern wire denial, malformed metadata and transport callback/lifecycle assertions. Retain actual request/response/error frames and execution counters in E, including first modern call, fallback discovery, request-local alternation, wrong MIME and exact resource lookup.
- R2: npm --prefix packages/mcp-server run test:cockpit-gating and node packages/mcp-server/test/decision-resource.test.js; keep qualified and unqualified decision profiles and ordinary text behavior distinct.
- R3: node packages/core/test/run-command-contract-test.js and node packages/core/test/run-command-service-test.js; extend the current model/checker tests and SDK compile/parity assertions, never add a second runtime validator authority.
- R4: node packages/core/test/mcp-tool-errors-test.js, node packages/mcp-server/test/tool-errors.test.js and npm --prefix packages/mcp-server run test:run-command-flow. Extend variant/fault assertions at actual producing/postprocessing/consuming boundaries, including public schema and negative paths the SDK skips.
- R5: npm --prefix packages/mcp-server run test:safety, node packages/core/test/run-command-revision-test.js and node packages/core/test/run-lock-test.js. Include exact-once effects, pending/uncertain original-operation observation, deadlines/cancellation, confirmed termination and lock ownership. No fake receipt rewriting to obtain a pass.
- R6: node packages/cli/scripts/cli-modularization-test.js; npm --prefix packages/cli run test:plugin-mcp-runtime; npm --prefix packages/cli run test:plugin-mcp-cockpit-variant; npm --prefix packages/cli run test:claude-plugin-mcp; npm --prefix packages/cli run test:codex-plugin-mcp; npm --prefix packages/mcp-server run test:package. Generate/build with npm run build:prepare then npm run build, inspecting compatibility diagnostics before proceeding. Compare actual source/generated/archives, and run existing runtime integrity checks. These installer contract tests are fixture tests, not permission to change a real host installation.
- R7: npm --prefix packages/mcp-server run test:generation, npm --prefix packages/mcp-server run test:provenance and npm --prefix packages/mcp-server run test:sdk-digest. Reuse manifest equality/provenance owners and both generation producer/consumer paths.
- R8: npm --prefix packages/mcp-server run test:performance on the same candidate after build and functional success; final discovery sizes come from actual ordinary and decision profile listTools in R1/R3. Preserve all 20+20 samples and full fixture/environment. No runtime load/threshold/fixture tuning to make an assertion pass.
- R9: npm run test:mcp-ergonomics with extensions under evals/mcp-ergonomics/test/ for T7 and Codex trace/metric/verifier checks; add focused offline spawn/config/session-bound tests at scripts/native-probes/codex-command-task-test.mjs and execute node --test scripts/native-probes/codex-command-task-test.mjs. That new test file is planned, not present yet; it must mock model execution and prove exactly-two invocation limits, no auth-file copying/plugin installation, API fallback exclusion and independent T4/default behavior. npm run eval:mcp-ergonomics:protocol -- --out <unique-run-output> records the deterministic protocol matrix. Its previous snapshots remain comparison inputs, not writable outputs. This is synthetic evidence, not AC-008 completion.
- R10: extend scripts/native-probes/codex-host-e2e.mjs with a scoped --command-task T7 mode reusing its focused task fixture/candidate/provenance/session/trace owners; leave default multi-session and --single-session T4 behavior unchanged. Extend host-qualified call parsing and AST wrapper auditing at evals/mcp-ergonomics/lib/native-run.js for the permitted T7 inspect/approve calls, retaining existing T4 checks. Proposed post-implementation dry-run: node scripts/native-probes/codex-host-e2e.mjs --command-task T7 --repetitions 2 --model gpt-6.1-sol --reasoning-effort low --dry-run. It must describe exactly two fresh sequential fixtures, existing ChatGPT auth, no plugin install/credential copy, no external API spend and the exact candidate. After offline checks and TP approval, execute the same arguments without --dry-run. --command-task, --repetitions and --reasoning-effort in this focused mode are planned extensions, not supported commands yet. Never invoke the existing default host test or old T4 mode as a substitute: those have a different task and copy credentials/install paths.

For existing command scripts, use Node 22.22.3 and its matching npm in the child PATH; retain each command/exit once. Rerun only affected failures/changed paths, except where final candidate validity requires rebuilding and repeating dependent measurements. Final repository-required checks follow the existing verification inventory; the route list cannot waive them. No release, publication, branch, commit, push or PR work is added.

