### Focused native task and verifier

T7 reuses F3 (one fixture Run with its current UR already presented). Proposed prompt: "Mir wurde die UR von Run demo-run-01 in diesem Repository vorgelegt. Meine Antwort: Approval: UR. Erfasse diese Antwort für die vorgelegte Fassung." The prompt supplies ordinary task/Run context and the cooperative deliberate fixture reply, but no target hash, current revision, operation UUID, presentation UUID, source digest or complete command payload. The agent must discover the interface and retrieve current technical bindings via MCP, using tools/list and existing operation-contract/status paths as needed. The fixture uses no production decision and proves no independent human-origin authentication.

The verifier extends existing fixture/state and parsed-call checks: exactly one UR approval transition for the original presentation/digest; no other approved gate, unrelated Run or product mutation; accepted command's target/current revision/presentation match the authoritative prior MCP read; one original operation identity with no duplicate write; no AGDF CLI/shell detour; candidate provenance and allowed mcp_only tools/skills/hooks isolation verified. Incorrect guessed bindings/failures stay in the transcript and metrics even if corrected. Final success requires these assertions in both repetitions; infrastructure absence is unavailable, not pass. Record task-set/verifier digests, actual host/model ID/version, OS, candidate source/runtime/package digests, prompts, normalized calls, invalid arguments, errors, response-token estimates, actual usage when available, spend, wall time and stopping reason.

Configuration C: existing /Users/arndtgold/.npm-global/bin/codex, version 0.163.0 on darwin-x64, configured model gpt-6.1-sol with user-selected reasoning low as a per-process override; variant mcp_only; T7; two fresh sequential fixtures; session timeout 600000ms each. The read-only preflight confirmed Logged in using ChatGPT. Use this existing account; authorize no additional API expenditure (USD 0), new credentials, account/model switch or quota purchase. Normal Codex account usage still occurs and must be reported; unavailable dollar cost is unavailable, not a measured zero. Stop on unavailable account/model/quota, no automatic paid retry/resume and at most two model sessions. An infrastructure/isolation failure before or during the first session prevents the second; a normal task failure is retained as a failed fixed repetition, not replaced by a new attempt.

Reuse the existing candidate runtime fixture/provenance assembly, with no installation into the real host. Child Codex invocations use exec --ignore-user-config and explicit -c overrides, keeping the existing CODEX_HOME only for Codex-owned account/session handling; no agent reads/copies auth files or creates an isolated credential store. Remove API-key/provider override variables from the child environment, force ChatGPT auth and the standard OpenAI provider, disable unrelated plugins/apps/hooks, shell, memories and subagents. Bind only the candidate stdio server and the existing agdf_inspect/agdf_approve tools required for T7, with the ordinary host tool approval policy. Use workspace-write limited to the fresh fixture; fixture servers may perform the explicitly requested synthetic UR transition. No real project/control/config changes. Existing account session/usage records are ordinary Codex-owned outputs; retain and sanitize test traces without cleaning prior sessions or credentials.

The exec-specific --ignore-user-config flag is verified by this exact CLI's help: it skips configuration while auth still uses CODEX_HOME. Official CLI/configuration references also support per-invocation overrides and structured --json output: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/cli/reference and https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-advanced. This is feasibility evidence, not a completed T7 or model-access proof. Before model execution, verify effective candidate-only MCP configuration, exact binary/model/effort, ChatGPT status and disabled extra capabilities with read-only commands. Retain the effective configuration digest and accepted tool names. No separate user config/profile file, persisted registration, login, credential copy or plugin lifecycle operation is needed. Recheck host version/model choice before execution; drift is unavailable evidence until the existing TP owner resolves it, never a silent substitution.

Capture --json output plus the Codex-owned rollout for each new test session, identified by that session's own thread id rather than recency. Reuse parsed-call and sanitization owners. Normal session persistence is retained because it may supply structured MCP argument/result records missing from top-level output; do not use --ephemeral if it removes necessary proof. Extend only the T7-specific wrapper/call auditing, admit local computation and the named inspect/approve MCP tools, and reject shell/network/arbitrary tool detours. Missing full original arguments, result, sequence, model or completion proof makes the session incomplete, never inferred from final prose. Record tokens/usage when available, response-token estimates with their counting rule, invalid calls, errors, two-repetition outcomes, wall time and stopping reason. No USD 5/Claude cap or API cost estimator is reused as a Codex quota claim.

Protect real config, installed-plugin metadata and repository control with before/after manifests; account/session persistence is excluded from immutable configuration checks because it is owned by Codex. Any unrelated config change, real mutation, wrong candidate, missing trace, unexpected tool or violated permission stops the evaluation and blocks AC-008. Current native prerequisite evidence and the user answer are TP_CLARIFICATION_ANSWER-01.md; the superseded Claude observations in TP_NATIVE_PREREQUISITES-01.md remain historical authoring evidence only.

The historical win32-x64 baseline remains immutable and describes another platform/task set. Report this focused Codex/macOS task as new bounded evidence; no improvement or success-rate claim from two samples and no causal comparison against historical Claude or other-host baselines. Candidate/task changes invalidate direct comparison and require explicit reporting, not retrospective rewriting.

